solution.p:
This equation has terms with denominators 4 and 11\text{.} The least common multiple of these is {44}\text{.} So the first step in solving this equation can be to multiply on each side by {44}\text{.}
\begin{aligned}
{44}\left({3x-{\frac{5}{11}}}\right) \amp= {44}\left({{\frac{9}{4}}x-12}\right)\\
{132x-20} \amp= {99x-528}\\
{132x-20+20} \amp= {99x-528+20}\\
{132x} \amp= {99x-508}\\
{132x-99x} \amp= {99x-508-99x}\\
{33x} \amp= {-508}\\
{x} \amp= {-{\frac{508}{33}}}
\end{aligned}
The solution set is {\left\{\frac{-508}{33}\right\}}\text{.}

